# The Schengen rule's twin — and proof it wasn't a one-off. Many countries
# make you tax-resident once you've spent 183 days there in a year. Same
# shape as 90-in-180, different numbers, the same one verb. Visa days, tax
# days, API rate limits, deploy quotas: they are all `rolling … limit`.

timezone = Europe/Lisbon

in_portugal = 2026-01-10 .. 2026-02-20,
              2026-04-01 .. 2026-06-15,
              2026-09-01 .. 2026-10-31

rolling days of in_portugal in 365 days limit 183          # peaks at 179
assert rolling days of in_portugal in 365 days limit 183   # holds — 4 days to spare
days of in_portugal & last 365 days                        # used so far this window

# stretch the last stay by a week and watch the assertion flip
